      "reviewer_notes": "All 3 gates passed: (1) Gate 1 \u2014 non-test caller exists at liquidate.move:229; (2) Gate 2 \u2014 no trust_assumptions in BUG_BOUNTY_SCOPE.json, gate cannot fire; (3) Gate 3 \u2014 contracts/protocol/sources/internal/market/market.move is explicitly in scope and 'liquidation logic' is a listed focus area. An attacker can trigger this via the ADL operator entry point (liquidate_adl_borrow) by invoking handle_debt_auto_deleverage on a qualifying obligation, causing liquidation_inner to call obligation.withdraw_ctokens(seized_ctokens) (market.move:776) and transfer the seized collateral to ctx.sender() (liquidate.move:254), violating INV-003 which asserts obligation.collateral_unchanged for ADLBorrow. Severity retained at High: direct protocol invariant violation enabling unintended collateral extraction from obligations during ADL operations.",
